##2.4 Extension: Spatial Durbin Model (optional/bonus)

#a)
sdm_fit = lagsarlm(lifeExp ~ log_gdp,
                   data = world,
                   listw = listw,
                   Durbin = TRUE,
                   zero.policy = TRUE)

summary(sdm_fit)
#The coefficient on the spatially lagged GDP variable (lag.log_gdp) is negative (-3.83) 
#and statistically significant (p < 0.001). This indicates that, controlling for a 
#country’s own GDP, higher GDP per capita in neighboring countries is associated 
#with lower life expectancy in a given country.

#b)
#The AIC of the SDM is 939.83, which is substantially lower than that of the SLM (967.93)
#and OLS (966), indicating a much better model fit despite the additional parameter.



